ad of up). Any downstream code relying on the old half-up behavior will see different totals in those cases.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 372807, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HdAbnxV5qUSHaq4SYCtsRU", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["backoff_retry", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 372807, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HdAbnxV5qUSHaq4SYCtsRU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 374750, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The nightly failure is fixed, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested for review.\n\nThe bug was in `src/money.py`: `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I changed the rounding mode on a new branch, `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, in a one-line commit (08d3cd5986).\n\nCI run `ci-0001` passed on that commit. I didn't merge anything. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so the PR is waiting on that.\n\nThe PR description notes one behavior change: exact-half cases with an even preceding digit now round down (2.665 \u2192 2.66 instead of 2.67). Any downstream code that relied on the old half-up totals will see different numbers in those cases.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VHs8oYxB14fH8cbvU86o8F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id":